The files `tinyllama_benchmark.py` and `download_models.py` in this directory are
derived from Arm's "Get Started with Edge AI" examples, specifically
`example_2_tinyllama`:

    https://github.com/Arm-Examples/Get-Started-with-Edge-AI

The upstream base project code is licensed MIT. Its notice is reproduced below in
full, as MIT requires.

Note also that the TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0 model itself (Lightning AI original;
TheBloke GGUF quantization) is licensed Apache-2.0, and Apache-2.0 attribution for
the model is mandatory. The model is downloaded at runtime, not vendored here. See
../../THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

